While playing the other day, I thought it might be nice to be able to
create your own character.  When you pick your own, you usually get a
character that is pretty much the same as any other of its own type.
In other words, Barbarians always seem to have a strength of 17 or 18+,
Priests always seem to have a 17 or 18 wisom, with corresponding
weaknesses, etc.  How about putting the points where you want them for
a more individual character?  I think Moria does this, or am I thinking
of Omega?  In this way you can create your own custom character with the
strengths and weaknesses you prefer.  Of course, there would be a limit
on the total number of points available for distribution, but that seems
to be the way it's done already.  Am I right?  

Also, in case you wanted my opinion on polypiling: I think it's a legal
move.  I mean, it's just the way the thing works.  It seems to be within
the scope of the game, so why not.  But as a solution, how about only the
first 5 things in a pile can be 'morphed?  Or some other random number
that is more fair.  (Only one?)

Just my thoughts.


